# "**/" makes each pattern match in every folder, not just the repo root.
# Without it, src/*/bin and src/*/obj would still be sent to the build.

# Why: host build output must never enter the image. Your Windows
# obj/project.assets.json would overwrite the Linux restore result.
**/bin
**/obj

# Why: .git is large and useless inside the image
.git
**/.vs

# Why: dev settings and secrets must not be baked into an image
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/.env

# Why: docs aren't needed to build or run
**/*.md

# Why: smaller context. Safe because we restore only the Web project, not the .sln
SchoolPortal.ArchTests/